        "id": null,
        "ref": "@verifyleader_documented_purpose",
        "kind": "behavior",
        "statement": "The documentation for VerifyLeader states that it is used to ensure the peer is still the leader and may be used to prevent returning stale data from the FSM after the peer has lost leadership. That is the promise the verification count is measured against: the call is offered as a leadership guard for reads, so a successful verification is read by callers as evidence that this node may still answer as leader, which is why it matters that the count it aggregates can be satisfied by sources the voter quorum does not contain.",
        "conditions": "This revision, the public VerifyLeader call as documented at the cited range; the statement records the documented purpose, and whether a given application relies on it that way is a property of the application.",
